---
import LegalPage from '../../components/pages/LegalPage.astro';
import { company, phoneLabel } from '../../data/company';
import { pagePath } from '../../i18n/ui';
---

<LegalPage lang="en" page="privacy" title="Privacy policy">
  <p>
    This is a translation for convenience. The <a href={pagePath('privacy', 'de')} lang="de">German version (Datenschutzerklärung)</a> is
    legally binding.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    {company.legalName}<br />
    {company.street}, {company.postalCode} {company.city}, Germany<br />
    Managing director: {company.ceo}<br />
    Phone: <a href={`tel:${company.phoneE164}`}>{phoneLabel('en')}</a><br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>
  </p>

  <h2>2. General information</h2>
  <p>
    We only process personal data to the extent necessary to provide a functional website, our content and our services. The legal bases
    are in particular Art. 6 (1) (a) (consent), (b) (contract and pre-contractual measures), (c) (legal obligation) and (f) (legitimate
    interests) of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>3. Hosting and delivery of the website</h2>
  <p>
    This website is delivered via Cloudflare, Inc. (USA). When you visit the website, Cloudflare processes technically necessary data,
    in particular your IP address, date and time of access, the page requested, referrer, browser and operating system. This serves the
    secure, stable and fast delivery of the website and protection against attacks. The legal basis is our legitimate interest under
    Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR.
  </p>
  <p>
    We have concluded a data processing agreement with Cloudflare. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework; data
    transfers to the USA are based on the European Commission's adequacy decision (Art. 45 GDPR) and additionally on the EU Standard
    Contractual Clauses. More information:
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cookies, tracking and fonts</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use cookies for analytics or advertising and do not use any tracking services. All fonts are loaded locally from our
    server; no connection is made to Google or other font providers.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Contact form</h2>
  <p>
    When you send us an enquiry via the contact form, we process your details (name, email address, your message and, optionally,
    company, phone number and requested service) to handle your enquiry. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR where your enquiry
    relates to a contract, and otherwise your consent under Art. 6 (1) (a) GDPR and our legitimate interest in answering enquiries under
    Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your message is delivered to our mailbox via the email service Resend (Resend, Inc., USA). Resend processes the data on our behalf
    under a data processing agreement. Transfers to the USA are based on appropriate safeguards, in particular the EU Standard Contractual
    Clauses.
  </p>
  <p>
    We delete your data once your enquiry has been fully handled, unless statutory retention obligations (e.g. under commercial or tax
    law) apply. You can withdraw your consent at any time with effect for the future, e.g. by email to
    <a href={`mailto:${company.email}`}>{company.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Spam protection with Cloudflare Turnstile</h2>
  <p>
    To protect our forms (contact and application form) against abuse by automated programs, we use Cloudflare Turnstile (Cloudflare, Inc., USA). Technical
    information such as your IP address and browser characteristics is transmitted to Cloudflare to check whether the input comes from a
    human. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in secure forms under Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR. For data transfers to the USA,
    see section 3.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Job applications</h2>
  <p>
    If you apply via our application form, we process your details (name, contact details, desired position and type of employment,
    qualification under Section 34a GewO, driving licence, languages, your message) and the documents you upload in order to review
    your application and carry out the application process. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR (steps prior to entering into an
    employment relationship).
  </p>
  <p>
    Your application is delivered to our mailbox via the email service Resend (see section 5) and is only made available to people
    involved in the selection process. If you are hired, we continue to process the data for the employment relationship. Otherwise we
    delete your application documents no later than six months after the application process has ended, unless you have consented to
    longer storage.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Contact by email or phone</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us by email or phone, we process your details to handle your request. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) or (f) GDPR.
    Section 5 applies accordingly to deletion.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right at any time to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access your stored data (Art. 15 GDPR)</li>
    <li>rectification of inaccurate data (Art. 16 GDPR)</li>
    <li>erasure (Art. 17 GDPR) and restriction of processing (Art. 18 GDPR)</li>
    <li>data portability (Art. 20 GDPR)</li>
    <li>object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR)</li>
    <li>withdraw consent with effect for the future (Art. 7 (3) GDPR)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). The authority responsible
    for us is the Bavarian State Office for Data Protection Supervision (BayLDA), Promenade 18, 91522 Ansbach, Germany.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Data security</h2>
  <p>This website uses TLS encryption. You can recognise an encrypted connection by “https://” in the address bar.</p>

  <h2>11. Last updated</h2>
  <p>September 2026</p>
</LegalPage>
